{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"abbb537a9a36237405cc1568909ad0f8c63473a8da57f7d5e3618503aa194d81","digest":{"component_or_area":"AWS shared infrastructure; terraform state management","key_entities":["arn:aws:iam::896586841071:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com","snap-demo-tfstate-896586841071","rebar-tfstate-896586841071","*.solutions.navateam.com","auth_host","rebar-terraform-plan","infra/terraform/iam.tf","Project tag"],"problem_keywords":["infrastructure migration","terraform state","resource ownership","OIDC provider","AWS","decommissioning"],"propositions":["Snap project is decommissioned but 18 shared AWS resources (OIDC provider, wildcard cert, auth_host SSO stack) remain orphaned in snap's dead terraform state and must be re-homed into rebar's state.","Rebar functionally depends on the GitHub OIDC provider singleton but does not own or create it; if snap's state is destroyed the provider is lost and rebar's drift CI role assumption breaks.","Adopted resources must preserve physical names (snap-demo-*) to avoid destroy/recreate churn but must have ownership and tags transferred from snap to rebar.","Live terraform import, apply, and retag must complete successfully with clean plan output and no unintended resource replacement or secret rotation.","Adopted resources must be removed from snap's shared state, added to rebar's terraform definitions, and verified via green terraform-drift CI after merge to main."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785824550292621940,"uuid":"f444a4d9-1bac-41a1-b00f-e8469dbdd507"}